"""Ladder part 1: the ladders (game/ladder.cpp) against the original's (script/ld_diff.cpp, suite ladder). Run: on
script/build_ld.bat, the full 1,500 cases; MUT_HARNESS script, MUT_EXTRA_SRCS original_exe.cpp and ld_calls.s,
MUT_LDFLAGS -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000; MUT_PASS "ld_diff: .*, N checks, 0 failures".

317 mutants, 32 not building; 239 of the 285 building killed at first, 247 after the test was widened (CanUse places
along the ladder's way, so that both ends answer true; a raised facing, a velocity with y 1, a speed of 0.0012, a frame
whose z axis is a tiny positive z). The 38 left:
- The port's fixes: the destructor frees a started ladder's volumes (99 del: the original's frees only the climbers'
  list, so the test stops each ladder first); the version of properties cut before it (168 num: the original goes on
  with a stack value, not given).
- Leaks, not observed: the volumes not deleted (106 del; 111 del).
- Float boundaries not reached: a square exactly 1e-8 (31 cmp; 43 cmp); squares exactly 1.5 (33 num; 41 num); the
  ends' squares equal (252 cmp); dot products, the speed and the height exactly at their limits (261 cmp; 263 cmp;
  265 cmp; 268 cmp; 272 cmp; 275 cmp; 277 cmp; 279 cmp).
- Equivalent: a float within 1e-8 of 1 is 1 (33 cmp; 41 cmp; 33 arith; 41 arith: no square is -1); a tiny speed taken
  as 1 still fails every test (32 num); the normalised vectors' y is 0 or unused (46 del; 46 arith; 66 num; 137 arith;
  245 del; 245 arith; 60 arith: the ladder's direction is level, its y only 1 when the ladder is vertical, whose
  dot products are 0 either way); a facing's y is not read (235 del; 235 num); a non-zero component's sign (49 cmp; 51
  cmp); sscanf answers -1, 0 or 1 and the id only when 1 (146 num; 148 num); the world matrix's fourth column is 0
  (200 cmp); the top volume set just after (211 del); the creator's registration answer unused (315 bool)."""
